{:fh/id  "FH-CTRL-003"
 :fh/law "A writable controller rendered with no :control address is refused loudly with :rf.error/view-control-address-missing naming the kind and the recovery — no default address, no synthesised one — while the same view given an address renders, and a props-only view that never asks for a record key is untouched."

 :kind :my.ui/buffered-field

 ;; The refusal. An absent :control is not defaulted: every controller
 ;; that skipped one would otherwise share a record keyed by nil.
 :missing-address-error-id :rf.error/view-control-address-missing
 :recovery                 :supply-a-control-address

 ;; The ex-data a programmer needs to locate the site: WHICH controller
 ;; family refused, and a bounded SHAPE summary of the props it was given
 ;; — never the props themselves.
 :extra-keys [:kind :props :reason :recovery]

 ;; The message names the prop and the recovery, so the fix is visible
 ;; without a debugger. Stable in MEANING, not in bytes — these are
 ;; substrings, not the message.
 :message-mentions [":control" "kind"]

 ;; The control for the refusal: the SAME view, given an address, renders.
 ;; Without this the rejection could be green because nothing renders.
 :control [:invoice 7 :amount]
 :value   "100.00"

 ;; And a props-only view never asks for a record key, so it has no
 ;; address to omit — the cost of controller addressing is paid only by
 ;; controls that actually write.
 :props-only-renders? true}
